400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 301 0 R
/E (India's macroeconomic backdrop remains robust but nuanced, anchored by real GDP growth of 7.4% in FY25 \(Q3 accelerating to 8.2% y-y\) and 7.0-7.3% projected for FY26, maintaining above-trend momentum. Industrial Production rose 7.8% y-y in December 2025, with Manufacturing PMI above 55 in January 2026, indicating continued factory expansion. WPI inflation moderated to +0.8% y-y, down sharply from peaks of 14.3% in FY23 \(through 6.0% in FY24, 1.5% in FY25\), signaling easing input-cost pressures, critical margin relief for cement manufacturers. Unemployment fell to 3.2% \(usual-status basis\), though urban unemployment hovers near 6.7-6.8%, highlighting labor-market frictions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
