402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 301 0 R
/E (Forex reserves at USD 600-620 billion provide buffer amid geopolitical tensions and U.S. tariff shocks, while the rupee remains relatively stable. Equity markets show resilience, Nifty 50 delivered 11-12% total return in FY25, supported by strong earnings and elevated foreign inflows. Sector rotation toward financials, industrials, and capex-linked names positions cement manufacturers like JK Cements favorably, as benign input costs and robust infrastructure spending create a supportive environment for margin expansion and volume growth.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 301 0 R
/E (India's economy is settling into a steady high-growth phase. Following a -23.1% contraction in FY21 and strong rebounds of 8.3% in FY22 and 7.2% in FY24, growth is stabilizing. While FY25 moderates to 6.5%, the projected rise to 7.4% in FY26 signals renewed momentum driven by robust domestic consumption, government capex, and sustained industrial activity.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9 10]
>>
endobj
