439 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 303 0 R
/E (JK Cement operates manufacturing plants across eight states in India. In Rajasthan, it has its flagship integrated grey cement plant at Nimbahera \(Chittorgarh, commissioned 1975\) and another integrated plant at Mangrol \(commissioned 2001\), both in Chittorgarh district, along with the country's first limestone-based White Cement plant at Gotan \(commissioned 1984\). In Karnataka, the integrated plant at Muddapur \(Bagalkot district\) has a capacity of 3.5 MnTPA. In Haryana, there is a split grinding unit at Jhajjar \(1.5 MnTPA\), and in Uttar Pradesh, grinding units operate at Aligarh \(1.5 MnTPA\), Hamirpur \(2 MnTPA, commissioned October 2022\), and Prayagraj \(3 MnTPA, commissioned June 2024\). Madhya Pradesh hosts an integrated plant at Panna \(2 MnTPA cement, commissioned November 2022\), a grey cement grinding unit at Katni \(2 MnTPA\), and another grinding unit at Ujjain \(1.5 MnTPA, commissioned November 2023\). In Gujarat, a grinding unit at Balasinor has a capacity of 0.7 MnTPA. In Odisha, acquired through Toshali Cement, there is an integrated unit at Koraput and a grinding unit at Cuttack. Most recently, in Bihar, a brand-new 3 MnTPA plant was commissioned at Buxar in January 2026, taking JK Cement's total grey cement capacity to 31.26 MnTPA across India )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
