/P 304 0 R
/T (The global cement industry is a critical pillar of infrastructure and construction activity worldwide. In 2025, the global cement market is estimated at approximately USD 430-440 billion, driven primarily by demand from residential construction, infrastructure development, and urbanization in emerging economies. Cement consumption remains closely correlated with GDP growth, public infrastructure spending, and housing demand, particularly in Asia-Pacific, which accounts for the largest share of global volumes.)
/E (The global cement industry is a critical pillar of infrastructure and construction activity worldwide. In 2025, the global cement market is estimated at approximately USD 430-440 billion, driven primarily by demand from residential construction, infrastructure development, and urbanization in emerging economies. Cement consumption remains closely correlated with GDP growth, public infrastructure spending, and housing demand, particularly in Asia-Pacific, which accounts for the largest share of global volumes.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
451 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 304 0 R
/T (The Asia-Pacific region dominates the global cement market, contributing nearly 60% of total consumption, led by China and India. Europe and North America together account for roughly 25-28%, while the Middle East & Africa and Latin America contribute the balance. The sector remains volume-driven, capital-intensive, and highly sensitive to energy costs and regulatory norms related to emissions and sustainability.)
/E (The Asia-Pacific region dominates the global cement market, contributing nearly 60% of total consumption, led by China and India. Europe and North America together account for roughly 25-28%, while the Middle East & Africa and Latin America contribute the balance. The sector remains volume-driven, capital-intensive, and highly sensitive to energy costs and regulatory norms related to emissions and sustainability.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
